# wsr-pal main_loop.pal - the REAL interactive human-playable loop
# (per direct instruction: human testability above all things). Reads
# keypresses from history.txt (keyboard_input.c writes them),
# dispatches every real key to wsr_menu_input.+x (which internally does
# BOTH digit-accumulation AND Enter-commit, matching mutaclsym's own
# proven title_input.c all-in-one design - simpler than muchi-pal-
# chat's own split buffer_key/send_message shape since there's no
# free-text entry here, only numbered-menu digits), then recomposes and
# hits the frame every tick, matching this whole family's proven
# 3-process (keyboard_input/prisc+x/renderer) shape.
#
# Note: read_history uses an INTERNAL file position that advances
# automatically on each call - the x1 register is a 0-based line
# offset we maintain in-register for crash-resume support via
# state.txt. update_history_cursor was formerly a separate opcode
# but is NOT recognized by prisc+x - instead we increment x1 in-
# register and persist it manually via write_state for resume support.
# When read_history returns 0 (no more pending keys), we halt - the
# persistent loop is handled by the caller (run_xod_agent.sh /
# button.sh sim-key background-and-kill pattern).
read_state x1, player_app history_cursor
li x3, 3
li x4, 1
compose_frame
hit_frame
loop:
read_history x2, x1
beq x2, x0, done
beq x2, x3, quit
wsr_menu_input x2
add x1, x1, x4
compose_frame
hit_frame
sleep 1000
j loop
done:
halt
quit:
halt
